78 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>At Take A Pause Live on Insight Timer over 5-6 September 2026, we practiced walking the path right here, right now, through mindfulness meditation. We then shared a reading from Erin Lee’s <a href=\"https://mindfulmoments.sg/books\">Take A Pause: Waking Up to a Life of Clarity</a>. </p><h3><strong>Meditation Practice</strong></h3><blockquote><p><em><strong>Tap Play to Practice Together:</strong></em></p></blockquote><div class=\"native-audio-embed\" data-component-name=\"AudioPlaceholder\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;label&quot;:null,&quot;mediaUploadId&quot;:&quot;67a12e7f-68d4-4fd3-a685-b63d44114211&quot;,&quot;duration&quot;:1303.3013,&quot;downloadable&quot;:false,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}\"></div><div class=\"captioned-button-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/the-path-beneath-our-feet?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CaptionedButtonToDOM\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">This post is free for some time, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. To support Erin’s work, upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.</p></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/the-path-beneath-our-feet?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/the-path-beneath-our-feet?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p></div>",
  "body_text": "Seven sessions into our Dhammapada series, we arrive at the chapter called The Path. The path here is the Noble Eightfold Path - right view, right intention, right speech, and the rest.\n\nThis is the path I have proclaimed, Having pulled out the arrows. It is up to you to make strong effort. Tathagatas merely tell you how. \n\n(verse 276, trans. Gil Fronsdal)\n\nTathagatas are those who have arrived at the truth. They tell you about the ‘how’, and that is all they can do. \n\nYou may revere your teacher and trust the teachings completely, and still the walking is yours and yours alone. Your teacher cannot walk the path for you.\n\nUnderstanding the path is not the same as standing on it. We can name everything that’s required for walking the path and still not have put our feet down. \n\nOnly when walking happens can the benefits of walking happen.\n\nWisdom arises from practice. Without practice, it decays.\n\n(verse 282, trans. Gil Fronsdal)\n\nCause and effect, stated plainly. Practice, and wisdom grows. Leave it, and knowledge stays knowledge, never becoming a true knowing.\n\nThe Buddha did not ask for these words to be believed. Ehipassiko, he said - come and see for yourself. So there is nothing here to take on faith. \n\nA path becomes a path only when it is walked.\n\nAnd there is no need to wait, for the path is right under our feet. \n\nIt is in everyday life — how we hold our minds this morning, in what our hands do today, in the words we offer the people in front of us. \n\nIt is also remarkably simple — do no harm, engage in what is skilful, and purify your own mind. \n\nMay we all start walking, and keep walking. \n\n---\n\nAt Take A Pause Live on Insight Timer over 5-6 September 2026, we practiced walking the path right here, right now, through mindfulness meditation. We then shared a reading from Erin Lee’s Take A Pause: Waking Up to a Life of Clarity. \n\nMeditation Practice\n\nTap Play to Practice Together:\n\nThis post is free for some time, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. To support Erin’s work, upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.\n\nShare",
